ggml-cpu gated delta net: one pass per state row instead of four sweeps

For each token the kernel swept the whole S_v x S_v f32 state (64 KB for Ling's KDA layers, S_v = 128) four times:
decay, dot with k, rank-1 update, dot with q. Each state row only needs its own data plus the shared k, q, g, v[j]
and beta, so this does all four steps per row while the 512-byte row is in L1. Each row sees the same operations in
the same order, so results do not change.
Correctness: KL divergence against stock at the tool's floor on x86 and on arm64 under QEMU (Ling, max 3.7e-5, same
top token 100%). Desktop x86, Ling: prefill +2.7%, decode about +5% (noisy). Phone speed: not measured yet.

